# `ab --job`: a whole job two ways.

[break] job-options-pass-without-job
rule: An option of a job A/B without --job is refused, not passed to nextest.
file: xtask/src/try_run.rs
in: job_words
find: if !asked {
replace: if false {
caught-by:
    try_run::tests::a_job_ab_is_test_job_with_against_and_its_options_go_to_ab_job

[break] job-ab-without-minutes
rule: A job A/B on a runner is given --minutes, so that it starts no round past the job's limit.
file: xtask/src/try_run.rs
in: job_ab
find: &JOB_AB_MINUTES.to_string()
replace: "0"
caught-by:
    try_run::tests::a_job_ab_is_test_job_with_against_and_its_options_go_to_ab_job

[break] job-round-starts-past-the-budget
rule: A round starts only when the longest round so far fits in the minutes left.
file: xtask/src/job_ab.rs
in: round_fits
find: spent_seconds + longest <= minutes as f64 * 60.0
replace: spent_seconds <= minutes as f64 * 60.0
caught-by:
    job_ab::tests::a_round_starts_only_when_the_longest_so_far_fits_in_what_is_left

[break] job-median-takes-failed-phases
rule: A failed phase is left out of its median.
file: xtask/src/job_ab.rs
in: medians
find: .filter(|phase| phase.name == name && phase.passed)
replace: .filter(|phase| phase.name == name)
caught-by:
    job_ab::tests::each_phase_takes_its_median_over_the_rounds_it_passed_in
    job_ab::tests::a_phase_no_round_passed_has_no_median_and_no_change

[break] job-failed-side-passes-the-run
rule: A side that failed fails the run, after the medians.
file: xtask/src/job_ab.rs
in: conclusion
find: if failed.is_empty() {
replace: if true {
caught-by:
    job_ab::tests::a_failed_side_is_shown_and_fails_the_run_and_a_clean_run_passes

[break] job-env-comments-are-variables
rule: A comment in the setup's environment file is passed over.
file: xtask/src/job_ab.rs
in: read_env
find: || line.trim_start().starts_with('#')
replace:
caught-by:
